<title>MEXICO: POLL - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen down to 18.01 pct.</title>
<headline>POLL - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen down to 18.01 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen falling 71 basis points to 18.01 percent, and rates are also seen falling at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     18.72	    18.01		   - 71 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     19.67	    19.12		   - 55 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    20.63	    20.05		   - 58 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     20.83	    20.03		   - 80 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 (2330 GMT)</p>
<p>((- Mexico City newsroom 525 728 9559))</p>
